# Check every text file out with LF on every platform.
#
# Git for Windows defaults to core.autocrlf=true, which rewrites LF to CRLF in the
# working tree. That turned the release archive built from a Windows checkout into a
# CRLF one, and lite/VERSION alone is enough to change the archive's SHA-256, so the
# same tag would have published two different bytes depending on who built it.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binaries carry no line endings to normalise.
*.png binary
*.webp binary
*.svg text eol=lf
*.wav binary
*.ico binary
